{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793607858,"nonce":"8e2k14mOEK42/Jajuys7y1SjLAI=","message":"Decided in the 2026-11-02 document review (design §11 updated to match).\n\n- **No recursion in M4.** Recursion over `int`/`long` is never structural, and no other M4 type (`bool`, enums, records) is inductive, so a structural-recursion translator would be untestable here. Recursive methods are rejected with a diagnostic, and the corpus contains one. Structural recursion moves to M5a, next to well-founded recursion.\n- **Theorem form.** In M4 a theorem is a parameterless `[Theorem]` method returning `Prove.That(\u003cbool expression\u003e)`. The translator closes it with `rfl`/`decide`. M5a adds parameters and `.By(...)`, which extends this form without breaking it. The M4 user API ships `[Verified]`, `[Theorem]`, `Prove.That` and only the `Spec.*` members M4 uses.","files":null}]}